                                "sense_id": "2d489237-5a07-3db1-8a66-b8cd596081f8",
                                "text": "Thus, in Naim v. Naim a white woman, married to a Chinese who was domiciled in Virginia, obtained an annulment of her marriage, which had been performed in North Carolina in order to evade Virginia's policy against miscegenetic unions."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
